@page "/faq"
@page "/FAQ.aspx"

<PageTitle>FAQ</PageTitle>

<section class="page-section narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
    <h1>Hurricane Tracking Software FAQ</h1>
    <p class="lede">The original FAQ was direct and practical. These are the main support answers long-time Tracking The Eye users relied on.</p>
</section>

<section class="faq-list narrow">
    <details open>
        <summary>How do I reinstall Tracking The Eye after a broken update or domain change?</summary>
        <p>Completely uninstall Tracking The Eye, make sure the old install directory is cleaned out, then reinstall from the latest setup package.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>I am getting a .NET or assembly load error. What should I do?</summary>
        <p>The legacy guidance was to reinstall the latest Microsoft .NET Framework because missing or corrupted framework components were a common cause of startup errors.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>I get an old MDAC version error. How do I fix it?</summary>
        <p>The original FAQ pointed users to the latest MDAC download from Microsoft because that error usually meant the machine was still using outdated data access components.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Does Tracking The Eye contain spyware or adware?</summary>
        <p>100% no. The original site was emphatic about this: Tracking The Eye is paid for by orders, not adware, and the servers are scanned constantly for these types of problems.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Is there a Mac version?</summary>
        <p>No desktop Macintosh version, but there has historically been an iPhone version available through the App Store.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>I lost my registration number. Where should I look first?</summary>
        <p>Look in the <strong>trackeye.ini</strong> file in your Windows directory. The original FAQ told users to open that file and check the Registration Info section for their saved name and number.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>What if I still cannot find my registration details?</summary>
        <p>Use the lost registration page or contact support with your name, address, phone number, original email address, approximate order date, and how you registered.</p>
    </details>
</section>
